🧠 DATA HUB 411: How to Build & Maintain a Scalable Anaplan Data Hub
  - A Data Hub is a centralized model that stores, cleanses, and distributes master and transactional data to spoke models
  - It is the backbone of an effective multi-model Anaplan architecture

📌 1. Purpose of the Data Hub
  - Single source of truth for master and transactional data
  - Decouples data ingestion from business logic
  - Reduces model size in spoke models through selective data transfer
  - Improves performance by minimizing redundancy and isolating transformation logic

📦 2. Key Components of a Data Hub
  Component	Purpose
    - Saved Views	Used to export cleaned or filtered data to spoke models
    - Import Staging Modules	Temporarily stores raw input from external systems
    - Transformation Modules	Performs mappings, filters, or value normalizations
    - Master Lists	Contains metadata and unique key hierarchies
    - Time Settings	May include SYS Time modules for tracking snapshot logic
    - Code-Driven Lists	Used for identifying records uniquely and efficiently
    - Export Actions	Scheduled exports or manual pushes to spoke models
    - Line Item Subsets (LISS)	Helps modularize calculations & versioning

⚙️ 3. Import Best Practices
  - Use code-based imports rather than name-based to maintain stability
  - Always import to flat lists first, then build hierarchies using system modules
  - Use numbered lists for large transactional data (e.g., employee records)
  - Include metadata columns (created date, source system, flags)
  - Create a SYS module per list for properties, hierarchy mapping, and filters

🧮 4. Example Module Structure
  📁 Modules
  ├── IMP01_Employee_RawData       (Staging)
  ├── SYS01_Employee_Properties    (Properties)
  ├── SYS02_Employee_Hierarchy     (Parent mapping)
  ├── EXP01_Employee_To_Spoke      (Export views)

🧰 5. Data Cleansing & Transformation
  - Remove blanks/nulls using boolean filters
  - Normalize text (e.g., UPPER, LOWER) for system consistency
  - Build mappings for:
    - Country → Region
    - GL Account → Reporting Category
    - Cost Center → Business Unit
    -- Include default/fallback logic in case mappings fail

🔁 6. Integration Flow
  - [Source System] → [Data Hub Staging Module] → [Cleaned SYS Module] → [Saved View] → [Spoke Model Import Action]
  - Use Anaplan Connect, MuleSoft, Boomi, or API integrations to automate file ingestion and distribution

🔒 7. Security & Access
  - Use minimal access roles — no business users should access the Data Hub directly
  - Set up model-to-model imports with dedicated integration users
  - Do not apply user-level access controls here; apply them in spoke models instead

📉 8. Performance Optimization
  - Avoid hierarchical lists unless needed — use flat lists and mapping modules
  - Use text list avoidance wherever possible
  - Use batch imports/exports during low-usage periods (off hours)
  - Archive old transactional data by exporting and purging based on snapshot logic

📤 9. Export Strategy
  - Export only what’s needed (e.g., filter on Current Period, Active Employees)
  - Version your exports using suffixes like _v1, _FY25, etc
  - Always name saved views clearly (EXP_ActiveEmployees_FY25)

🧪 10. Validation & Testing
  - Build QA dashboards in the Data Hub for:
    - Record counts vs source system
    - Delta checks (last import vs current)
    - Invalid mappings or blanks
    - Automate error logging (e.g., unmapped items, duplicates)

🧠 Pro Tips
  - Use ALM wisely: Treat the Data Hub as non-production unless it contains business logic
  - Minimize logic: Push logic to spoke models unless it applies to all downstream models
  - Snapshot modules: Store time-based versions for comparison (e.g., prior month employee list)
